## Chapter 6: The Shadows of Sector 7
The acrid smell of burning ozone and scorched iron hung heavy over Sector 7’s rail yard.
Farther down the tracks, Vance—the arrogant Tier-B Flame Striker from Gideon Prep—was shouting orders, his hands flickering with weak, desperate spouts of flame as his squad tried to drive back the two remaining Iron-Claw Raptors. They had no idea that the largest beast of the pack had already been slaughtered in the shadows behind them, its corpse turned to fine gray ash, its pure Tier-D core devoured and integrated into Kaelen's nervous system.
Kaelen crouched in the dark space beneath a rusted freight car, fifty meters away from the fighting.
He lowered his head, pressing his back against the iron axle, and let his breathing become deliberate and shallow. He deliberately loosened his jaw, allowed his shoulders to slump, and smeared a streak of greasy black mud across his left cheek.
To anyone looking at him right now, he was just another terrified Tier-E auxiliary student hiding from monsters he had no hope of fighting.
Underneath the filthy uniform, however, Kaelen's body was humming with terrifying density.
His muscles felt tight and packed like coiled spring steel. The newly integrated **[Obsidian Carapace]** trait sat quietly beneath his skin, ready to harden his sub-dermal tissues at a microsecond's notice. Deep in his forearms, the energy of his newly stolen active skill—**[Iron-Claw Burst]**—throbbed like a dormant engine.
*Focus,* Kaelen told himself, closing his eyes. *Suppress it. Bring the pulse down.*
He channeled his focus inward, forcing his elevated heart rate back down to a baseline 60 beats per minute. He allowed the surge of raw stats—**26 Strength, 27 Agility, 28 Vitality**—to settle deep into his core, locking it behind the fragile mask of a Level 3 Salvager.
*Wroooaar!*
A sharp, metallic shriek echoed across the yard, followed by the heavy, dull thud of an explosion. Vance had finally managed to detonate an auxiliary fuel canister, incinerating one of the Raptors while the other retreated back into the dense, fog-covered treeline.
"Area secure! Perimeter clear!" a stern voice shouted over the squad frequency.
Instructor Horgan stepped through the haze, his heavy combat boots crunching over shattered gravel. His cybernetic left arm was extended, the integrated sensory scanner whirring as it swept the rail yard for lingering threat signatures.
Vance was leaning against a boxcar, gasping for air, his pristine silver-trimmed armor scuffed and covered in black soot.
"We... we repelled the ambush, Instructor," Vance panted, trying to straighten his posture and regain his aristocratic composure. "One beast destroyed by my flame artillery, one killed by the fuel detonation, and the third fled back into the zone."
Horgan stopped, his mechanical eye zooming in on the dark stain on the ground where the fuel canister had exploded, then shifting toward the dark corner under the freight car where Kaelen was huddled.
Horgan walked over, his heavy limp echoing against the iron tracks. He stopped in front of the freight car and looked down.
"Vance," Horgan said, his gravelly voice devoid of any warmth. "Get out from under there."
Kaelen flinched deliberately, looking up with wide, trembling eyes. He scrambled backward through the mud before slowly pulling himself to his feet, keeping his head low and his hands shaking slightly.
"S-Sir," Kaelen stammered, making his voice sound breathy and shaken. "The... the big one. It lunged at me. I threw a heavy supply crate at its head and ran..."
Horgan didn't interrupt. He stepped closer, his cybernetic eye emitting a narrow red grid-scan that swept over Kaelen's body from head to toe.
**[External Scanning Signal Detected...]**
**[System Mask Active: Displaying Public Interface Profile.]**
 * **Identity:** Kaelen Vance (Student ID: AV-8809)
 * **Class:** Salvager (Tier-E)
 * **Visible Attributes:** Suppressed to Tier-E Baseline Thresholds.
The red light vanished. Horgan’s scowl deepened, but his expression remained unreadable.
"You're lucky the beast was distracted by the crate," Horgan said gruffly. "A Tier-E taking a direct hit from an Iron-Claw Raptor ends up in a body bag. Next time, don't wander off from the supply line."
"Yes, sir. Understood, sir," Kaelen muttered, pulling his arms in close and looking down at his muddy boots.
Vance sneered from across the tracks, wiping sweat from his forehead. "Typical Anvil Ridge trash. Give them a job to carry boxes and they hide under a train at the first sign of a fight."
Kaelen didn't respond. He kept his eyes fixed on the ground, letting Vance's words bounce off him like rain on stone. Let them think he was a coward. Let them mock him. Every insult was just more concrete pouring over his secret foundation.
"Cut the noise, cadet," Horgan barked at Vance, turning on his heel. "Gideon squad, secure the perimeter boundary. Anvil Ridge team, clean up the rail yard. Salvage the scrap, pack the sensor units, and prepare the transport."
For the next two hours, while the Gideon cadets stood guard looking heroic for the municipal drone cameras, Kaelen and his classmates worked in the mud, hauling broken gear and heavy iron cables.
Kaelen picked up a jagged two-hundred-pound section of shattered train rail that had been blasted off by the explosion. To make it look believable, he let out a loud groan, locking his elbows and faking a strain as he dragged it toward the recovery truck.
In reality, he was barely using 10% of his **26 Strength**.
While dragging the metal, he passed the dark spot where he had deconstructed the Tier-D Raptor. The ash had already been scattered by the wind, leaving zero trace of the monster's remains.
He pulled up his interface in the quiet corners of his mind, reviewing his newly evolved skill:
**[Dissect & Assimilate (Lv. 1)]**
 * **Active Skill Stored (1/1):** [Iron-Claw Burst (Tier-D)]
 * *Next Skill Slot Unlocks at:* Class Evolution / Tier-D Conversion.
*One stored active skill slot,* Kaelen thought, his eyes narrowing as he tossed the heavy rail onto the truck bed. *I need to be extremely selective about what I steal next.*
[Iron-Claw Burst] gave him a devastating physical armor-piercing strike, but he lacked long-range capability, stealth concealment, or defensive barriers. He needed to target specific monster types during his midnight hunts to build a completely rounded, unstoppable combat kit.
When the sun began to dip below the heavy industrial smog of Sector 7, the transport trucks rumbled back toward Anvil Ridge Vocational.
Kaelen sat in the back of the cold metal truck, leaning his head against the rattling side panel. Beside him, his classmates were complaining about their aching muscles, their ruined boots, and the petty tyranny of the Gideon Prep students.
Kaelen closed his eyes and listened to the rhythmic thrum of the truck's engine.
He wasn't tired. His **28 Vitality** meant his body recovered from physical strain almost instantly.
He felt the hidden power coursing beneath his skin—a silent, lethal engine sitting in the dark, waiting for the night to fall.
*Tonight,* Kaelen thought, his fingers curling tightly inside his pockets as the truck crossed into the slum district. *Sector 9 subway tunnels. Time to hunt for something with range.*
